        "doc_id": "1770402787374248000_0",
        "from_clapnq": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1770402787373407000_0_535",
      "text": "In the playoffs, Belfour posted three shutouts in the opening round against the Senators, setting a record for shutout streaks in a series. However, in the second round, former teammate Jeremy Roenick eliminated the Leafs by putting a game 6 overtime goal past Belfour.\nBelfour did not play during the NHL lockout in 2004\u201305, instead taking a minority stake in the projected Dallas Americans team in the proposed revival of the World Hockey Association while recovering and rehabilitating himself from primarily back-related injuries. The team had folded by October, 2004.\nOn November 28, 2005, Belfour won his 447th career NHL game, moving him into a tie with Terry Sawchuk for 2nd place in career wins. Ed made 34 saves in the 2\u20131 win over the Florida Panthers.\nOn December 19, 2005, Belfour moved past Sawchuk with a 9\u20136 win over the New York Islanders at the Air Canada Centre. He was honoured in a special pre-game ceremony on December 23, 2005, before a game against the Boston Bruins at the Air Canada Centre; the Leafs went on to win the game.",
